# Backend (Porto)

Do not use `app/Http/Controllers`. One feature lives in one container.

```
app/Containers/{Section}/{Name}/
  UI/API/Routes/{Verb}{Name}.v1.private.php  → Action::class
  UI/Actions/{Verb}{Name}Action.php          → asController + handle
  UI/API/Requests/*Request.php
  UI/API/Transformers/*Transformer.php
  Tasks/{Verb}{Name}Task.php                 → run()
  Data/DTO/*Dto.php                          → extends App\Ship\Parents\DTO\Data
  Data/Repositories/*Repository.php
  Models/
  Tests/{Unit,Functional}/
app/Ship/  → shared parents, middleware, helpers only
```

- `<?php declare(strict_types=1);` on line 1. Extend Ship parents (`BaseAction`, `Task`, `AuthenticatedRequest` / `PublicRequest`).
- Route file: `Route::{verb}('resource', Action::class)->middleware(['auth:api']);` — auto-loaded, prefix already `api` + `/v1`.
- Action: inject Task; `asController(Request $r): JsonResponse`; DTO via `XDto::from([...$r->validated(), 'user_id' => auth()->id()])`; return `fractal($m, new XTransformer())->withResourceName('...')->addMeta([...])->respond(...)`.
- Task: inject repository; no HTTP. Repository: Eloquent / `App\Ship\Parents\QueryBuilder\QueryBuilder`.
- Tests next to the container. Functional HTTP: `/api/v1/...`, `actingAs($user, 'api')`.
- Unhandled exceptions must stay JSON (see `ConfigureExceptions`). Do not render Ignition HTML for API.
